	(text "The video card V4.0, one sheet per functional block:\n  sheet 2  Bus and ports BUS INTERFACE: THE BLOCK SELECT, THE SIX PORTS' STROBES, THE TWO CONTROL REGISTERS, THE STATUS\n  sheet 3  CRTC and clock THE 6845, THE DOT CLOCK, THE DOT COUNTER, THE 6845'S CLOCK, THE STAGE REGISTERS\n  sheet 4  Text         THE TEXT RAM, THE CODE REGISTER, THE CHARACTER GENERATOR, THE TEXT SHIFTER, THE CURSOR FLAG\n  sheet 5  Graphics RAM THE GRAPHICS RAM: ADDRESS MULTIPLEXERS, WRITE BUFFER, THE TWO READ PATHS, BYTE LATCH, SHIFTER\n  sheet 6  Slots        THE SLOT LOGIC: SELCPU, THE WRITE FLIP-FLOP, THE -WE PULSE, THE RAM'S -OE, THE READ LATCH'S CLOCK\n  sheet 7  Dots and syncs THE TWO LAYERS MIXED, THE DOT RETIMED, THE THREE GUNS, THE SYNCS, THE VGA SOCKET\n  sheet 8  PS2          PS/2: ATMEGA328P, LATCHES ON PD / PE, STATUS, FTDI, -INT, RESET\n  sheet 9  Power        POWER UNITS, DECOUPLING, POWER LED, THE F PARTS' PULL-UP\n\nEvery net of a sheet is a pin of its sheet symbol here, and the local label at each pin names the net\n(/NAME, the names on the board). Above the dashed line: the nets the sheet shares with other sheets (left:\nit reads them, right: it drives them). Below it: the nets drawn on that sheet only, a pin on each side\n(KiCad's ERC counts a root label as connected only when another label of its name is on the root sheet).\nVCC and GND are power symbols on the sheets." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 15.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cfcecaf4-0f85-54f2-8a39-1d8acbab9d5f"))
	(sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
